---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
---

<Policy
  title="Cancellation Policy | India Visit"
  heading="Cancellation policy"
  description="How cancellations, amendments and refunds work on journeys arranged by India Visit."
  path="/cancellation/"
>
  <h2 id="scope">What this covers</h2>
  <p>
    Journeys we arrange ourselves. <strong>Luxury trains are different</strong> —
    they are operator-run on fixed departures, and their cancellation slabs are
    set by the operator. Those are published separately in our
    <a href="/booking-terms/">booking terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="notice">Cancellation by you</h2>
  <p>
    The slab structure — how much is retained at each notice period — is the
    client's commercial decision and must be stated here as a table, not as
    prose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="amendments">Amendments</h2>
  <p>
    What can be changed after confirmation, by when, and what a change costs.
  </p>

  <h2 id="by-us">Cancellation by us</h2>
  <p>
    The circumstances in which we would cancel, and what happens to money
    already paid.
  </p>

  <h2 id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
  <p>How a refund is issued and how long it takes.</p>

  <h2 id="force-majeure">Force majeure</h2>
  <p>To be settled by the client's legal adviser.</p>
</Policy>
